# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, a clone on Windows (core.autocrlf=true, the Git for Windows
# default) checks every text file out with CRLF, while Prettier is configured
# for LF. The result was `npm run lint` reporting ~49,000 `Delete ␍` errors on a
# clean checkout — enough to make the lint gate useless and to hide real
# findings behind noise.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository AND on checkout, on
# every platform, so the working tree matches what Prettier and CI expect.
# Windows editors handle LF fine; this is the standard arrangement for a
# cross-platform repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must keep CRLF to run on Windows.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries — an eol conversion corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
